    {
      "text": "#### how Hadoop Framework work\n- The fundamental idea of YARN is to split up the functionalities of resource management and job scheduling/monitoring into separate daemons. The idea is to have a global ResourceManager (RM) and per-application ApplicationMaster (AM). An application is either a single job or a DAG of jobs.\n\nThe ResourceManager and the NodeManager form the data-computation framework. The ResourceManager is the ultimate authority that arbitrates resources among all the applications in the system. The NodeManager is the per-machine framework agent who is responsible for containers, monitoring their resource usage (cpu, memory, disk, network) and reporting the same to the ResourceManager/Scheduler.\n\nThe per-application ApplicationMaster is, in effect, a framework specific library and is tasked with negotiating resources from the ResourceManager and working with the NodeManager(s) to execute and monitor the tasks.\n\n[hadoop_doc](https://hadoop.apache.org/docs/stable/hadoop-yarn/hadoop-yarn-site/YARN.html)\n\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "dfc84e6c74674c148843e"
    },
    {
      "text": "####SaveMode\n**default is errorIfExists.**\n\n1.  SaveMode.append  : *Appends the output files to the list of files that already exist at that location*\n2.  SaveMode.Overwrite:  *Will completely overwrite any data that already exists there*\n3.  saveMode.errorIfExists: *Throws an error and fails the write if data or files already exist at the specified location.* \n4.  SaveMode.Ignore: *If data or files exist at the location, do nothing with the current DataFrame*",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "761a6719915a4037b00d4"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.types.{StructType,StructField,StringType,IntegerType,DoubleType}\n\nval data =  Seq(\n  Row(\"Ram\", 23, 12121.0),\n  )\n\nval myManualSchema = StructType(Array(\nnew StructField(\"name\", StringType, true),\nnew StructField(\"age\", IntegerType, true),\nnew StructField(\"salary\", DoubleType, false)))\n\nval rdd = spark.sparkContext.parallelize(data,2) \nval df = spark.createDataFrame(rdd,myManualSchema)\nimport spark.implicits._\nval seqdf = Seq((\"Ram\",24,111)).toDF()\n\nspark.creat",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "3757784d05b644849955e"
